Package: starlock-headless
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Kyle Downs <12downsk@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.36), libjpeg62-turbo, adduser
Conflicts: pushnav-headless
Replaces: pushnav-headless
Section: science
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/kwdowns/starlock
Description: Starlock plate-solving push-to for Raspberry Pi (headless)
 Starlock plate-solves live frames from a finder camera to show where a
 manual telescope is pointing and guide it to a target (push-to).
 .
 This is the headless Raspberry Pi build: it runs as a systemd service
 with no window, and is controlled from a phone or laptop browser at
 http://<pi-ip>:8780. SkySafari / Stellarium Mobile connect over LX200
 on port 4030, Stellarium desktop on port 10001.
 .
 It bundles its own Python 3.12 runtime under /usr/lib/starlock-headless.
 Starlock is a fork of PushNav and replaces the pushnav-headless package.
 For a PC or laptop, use the regular Starlock desktop release instead.
